# Case of the Pilfered Proof: "Solved — If one or more tokens would be created under your control, those tokens plus a Clue token are created instead." (CR 614.1a, 702.169b). The Case
# is solved at the end of Bot1's turn 5 (three Novice Inspectors, as in the solving scenario), and every investigate before then made one Clue: 12 permanents (five Moxen, the Case, three
# Inspectors, three Clues). On turn 6 Bot2's own Novice Inspector makes its one Clue and no more, tokens not under Bot1's control. On turn 7 Bot1's Inside Source makes its 2/2 Detective
# token and the Case adds one Clue to that event: Source, token and Clue make 15 permanents, and the token has the Case's +1/+1 counter, a 3/3.

